# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PETSc solver options for JOREK.
#
# Copy this file to  jorek.petsc  in the run directory and uncomment what you
# need. It is read automatically at startup when present; if it is absent JOREK
# runs with its built-in defaults, which are exactly the settings listed as
# "default:" below.
#
# Format is the standard PETSc options file: one option per line, '#' comments.
# Anything set here overrides JOREK's compiled-in default.
#
# Three prefixes exist:
#   -jorek_          the main iterative (GMRES) solve
#   -jorek_pcblock_  the direct solver inside every preconditioner block
#   -jorek_direct_   the one-shot direct solve path
#
# The -jorek_pcblock_ prefix is shared by all toroidal mode-family blocks, so a
# single option below reconfigures every one of them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Main iterative solve ---------------------------------------------------
# -jorek_ksp_type            gmres      # default: gmres
# -jorek_ksp_rtol            1e-8       # default: 1e-8
# -jorek_ksp_max_it          400        # default: 400
# -jorek_ksp_gmres_restart   40         # default: 40
# -jorek_ksp_view                       # dump the full solver configuration
#
# Note: the outer preconditioner is always PCFIELDSPLIT. It carries the toroidal
# mode-family decomposition, so -jorek_pc_type is not a supported knob.

# --- Direct solver used in each preconditioner block ------------------------
# Which factorization package. Requires the package in your PETSc build;
# PETSc reports clearly at startup if it is missing.
# -jorek_pcblock_pc_factor_mat_solver_type mumps          # default
# -jorek_pcblock_pc_factor_mat_solver_type superlu_dist
# -jorek_pcblock_pc_factor_mat_solver_type strumpack
# -jorek_pcblock_pc_factor_mat_solver_type cudss          # GPU
#
# Note: PETSc's built-in LU ('petsc') is NOT usable here - the blocks are MPIAIJ
# and it only factorizes SEQAIJ. PETSc says so clearly if you try.
#
# MUMPS controls. JOREK's defaults are ICNTL(7)=7 (METIS ordering),
# ICNTL(14)=50 (workspace %), ICNTL(8)=77 (auto scaling), ICNTL(22)=0 (in-core).
# Setting one here overrides just that one; the rest keep JOREK's values.
# -jorek_pcblock_mat_mumps_icntl_22 1    # 1 = out-of-core factorization
# -jorek_pcblock_mat_mumps_icntl_7  5
#
# SuperLU_DIST / STRUMPACK / cuDSS controls follow the same pattern:
# -jorek_pcblock_mat_superlu_dist_colperm PARMETIS
# -jorek_pcblock_mat_strumpack_compression NONE
#
# The block solver itself can also be replaced wholesale, e.g. to try an
# iterative block solve instead of a direct one:
# -jorek_pcblock_ksp_type richardson
# -jorek_pcblock_pc_type  hypre

# --- One-shot direct solve path ---------------------------------------------
# -jorek_direct_pc_factor_mat_solver_type mumps           # default

# --- Diagnostics ------------------------------------------------------------
# -options_left                         # report unused (i.e. misspelled) options
# -log_view                             # PETSc performance summary
